Q1 – Sorting Under Different Data Conditions

Problem Context

E-Commerce Order Processing

Aim

To implement Selection Sort, Bubble Sort and Insertion Sort and compare their performance under different input conditions.

Algorithms Used

Selection Sort
Bubble Sort
Insertion Sort
Test Datasets

Nearly sorted data
Randomly ordered data
Reverse sorted data
Empty list
Performance Measures

Number of comparisons
Number of swaps or movements
Execution time
Time Complexity

Algorithm| Best Case| Average Case| Worst Case Selection Sort| O(n²)| O(n²)| O(n²) Bubble Sort| O(n)| O(n²)| O(n²) Insertion Sort| O(n)| O(n²)| O(n²)

Observation

Insertion Sort performs efficiently when the input is nearly sorted. Bubble Sort can stop early when the data is already sorted. Selection Sort performs approximately the same number of comparisons regardless of the input arrangement.

Recommendation

Insertion Sort is recommended for the given e-commerce scenario because approximately 95% of existing orders are already sorted and only small batches of new orders are added.

Result

The three sorting algorithms are implemented and compared using different datasets. The final recommendation should be supported by the operation counts obtained from program execution.
